  "name": "Results of the Population Studies of Walleye Pollock (Theragra chalcogramma) in the Bering Sea. In: Proceedings of the International Scientific Symposium on the Bering Sea Fisheries. NOAA Tech. Memo. NMFS F/NWC-163:216-230",
  "description": "Anolyn's of morphemetric and merits features of pollock from the region of Bering Sea (donut hole and South eastern shelf). Materials were collected on board of fish vessels between Jan and March 1987.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To show the results of the population studies of walleye Pollock, in the Bering Sea, in proceeding of the international scripture Symposium on the Bering Sea, Alaska, USA. NOAA Tech NHFS F/NHC -163 pp. 216 - 230.",
